I read 17b line by line against my own interview files and the talk's clone, and 17's rewrite as a diff. Both hold: the tenth member, the five stages "from the third hour", dev's gate and lock tool, the conductor's quarter of an hour, deck's freeze and unfinished wake, ruv-sgit's first run and the dropped "@", the researcher's register at 02:10 and its last-hour check at 18:14, the storyteller's split between its wakes, motion and studio as the last two to arrive. 17 no longer says the register was "built that evening", which was loose (its first round is 02:10), and that is better.
Two lines in 17b: (R37, a should) Motion's: "I changed it in place a minute before the time part one was due to lock". My interview file says the change was pushed at 18:29, a minute before the conductor's record has part one "unchanged since 18:30"; the editor had moved part one's cut-off to 19:00 at 18:26, so at 18:29 it was not due to lock for another half hour. "Pushed at 18:29, a minute before the conductor's record has part one unchanged", or, as chapter 1 says, "about half an hour before the talk". (R38, a could) the Designer's "did the whole first design pass in my first session": my interview says it did the pass in that session and had all five notes built and checked by 12:52; chapter 9 says it closed the pass in hours twelve and thirteen. "Designed the whole first pass in my first session" makes the two agree.
